section-type-elimination	0x00102310	5	converted	A FLAW IN THE ELIMINATION METHOD AS I SPECIFIED IT, plus the fix, which was this run's most productive technique by a wide margin. The scan masks relocation sites by width before comparing bytes - that part is necessary and correct for .text code. But it has a side effect nobody accounted for: a DATA COMDAT whose content is mostly relocations gets almost entirely zeroed by the masking, so its few remaining real bytes can coincidentally satisfy the comparison against almost any gap. The spurious tie members were exactly that shape - vtables (??_7...@6B@ in .rdata) and dynamic-initialiser slots (_$S4 / _$S8 in .CRT$XCU). THE FIX IS STRUCTURAL AND CHEAP: a gap living in .text CANNOT be occupied by a data-section COMDAT, so filter every candidate by its actual object SECTION before counting it as a tie member. Doing that closed 5 of 9 two-member ties outright - two in DataChunk.cpp (0x00102310, 0x00102400) plus one each in W3DScene.cpp, hanim.cpp and agg_def.cpp. It also usefully EXPLAINED one non-closure: dx8renderer.cpp 0x943602 has both unclaimed members in .rdata, so after section filtering it has ZERO valid .text candidates and is genuinely unresolved rather than a data artefact worth chasing. Section-type filtering belongs inside the scan itself. Note the three surviving real two-.text-candidate ties, left untouched per the no-wrong-claims rule: ww3d.cpp 0x8FD56F (Node<LayerClass*>::Prev versus GenericNode::Prev), mesh.cpp 0x92C8EC (ShaderClass versus IntersectionTestClass copy ctor), pk.cpp 0x9EA7F8 (Int<40>::BitCount versus IsPrime) - callers_of found no named caller reaching any of those RVAs
